    aboutHashHow: 'To check: on Windows run certutil -hashfile <installer file> SHA256 in Command Prompt, on a Mac run shasum -a 256 <installer file>; the result must match the value above exactly.',
    about: 'About', version: 'Version {v} (2026-10-05)',
    relNotes: [{"v": "3.0.1", "items": ["All five chains are equal. The chain with 0x addresses is now called EVM or Shard0 (EVM), for example \"EVM accounts\" and \"EVM graphics card\".", "Installs over 3.0.0 and 2.0.12 and keeps your accounts and settings."]}, {"v": "3.0.0", "items": ["Shard1–4 and Shard0 (EVM) can mine together, using the graphics card and the processor in any combination. The mining programs run at a lower priority so the window stays smooth. The name stays SCDO Wallet and this release installs over 2.0.12.", "Each account card adds Mining and Send beside Rename, Hide and Delete. The click opens that feature with this account already selected.", "The top status bar only shows information: each chain's sync, time left, mining speed, graphics-card temperature colour, today's earnings, total earnings, the account balance, and connected nodes. The ? explains each item. The row below has only buttons: Start mining, Open the mining page, Send, and Stop all, which asks you to confirm first. There is no separate network menu, and the Classic accounts tab is first.", "AI小貓 sits in a corner and can be turned off in Settings. It uses on-device rules only: one-tap mining (it stops the graphics card above 85°C and says so), a node restart when sync stalls or there are no peers, balance answers, a keyfile backup walkthrough that never shows a seed, and filling in a form from a short sentence typed in Chinese, such as \"send 100 to someone\". It never signs or sends; you confirm that yourself.", "Sending and remittance are now one entry: Send. Type an address, a saved name, or a remit payee plus an amount, and the wallet picks the route: a 0x or Classic address is an on-chain transfer on that shard, and a remit payee or a fiat amount uses the remit gateway. The route is one line. Nothing is signed or sent until you press confirm. Account tabs still show balances. Each card and the button row below keep a single Send button. The separate send buttons and the remit tab are removed."]}, {"v": "2.0.12", "items": ["New Remittance entry (now called Send) on Home, the tab bar and the menu; unlock the current account and sign in to the remittance gateway; you only see your own address's ledger and another address cannot sign in; no identity form"]}, {"v": "2.0.11", "items": ["Mining page copy: yellow card when there is no graphics card (tap Run a node to start + register rewards), external-node, and node reward-address messages"]}, {"v": "2.0.10", "items": ["When you switch to 華語, the menu bar becomes Traditional Chinese", "Send/mining address and amount: full-width characters are normalised to half-width before checks"]}, {"v": "2.0.9", "items": ["Top bar no longer wraps in a narrow window"]}, {"v": "2.0.8", "items": ["Main colour is now light green"]}, {"v": "2.0.7", "items": ["Mining notifications: first accepted share or block found, pool payout received, hashrate stuck at 0, mining stopped by something other than you, local node behind; each one can be turned off in Settings", "Pool mode: the Mining tab shows pool payouts - unpaid balance against the payout minimum, the last payout and its transaction", "Settings: choose the update channel - Stable (default) or Beta", "About shows the SHA-256 of this version's installer, to compare with the .sha256 file on the download page"]}, {"v": "2.0.6", "items": ["The window and the mining status show up right away after an update or at start - no more black window", "The top bar always shows mining: on or off, hashrate and pool", "The ✕ at the top right hides the wallet to the tray and mining keeps running; to quit, choose Quit on the tray icon", "Stopping mining now asks you to confirm first", "After an update the window title says it was updated", "When an update check fails, the message tells you whether it was the connection or the update information that failed its check"]}, {"v": "2.0.5", "items": ["New language button (Chinese / English) next to the settings button at the top: switch the language with one click", "Mining: the official SCDO pool is filled in by default; you can change it to another pool", "Release notes are now listed by version, one change per line", "Places in the Chinese interface that still showed English are now translated", "Tokens in the asset list are now labelled \"EVM token\""]}, {"v": "2.0.4", "items": ["Switch the language between English and 繁體中文 in Settings; your choice is remembered", "The Mining tab and the transfer confirmation are translated too"]}, {"v": "2.0.3", "items": ["The Chinese interface is now Traditional Chinese", "Account backups are saved in the Documents\\ScdoWallet\\備份 folder"]}, {"v": "2.0.2", "items": ["Activity now lists incoming transfers", "Several transfers sent one after another no longer fail", "Send all leaves nothing behind", "Clear message when you are offline", "Amounts are never rounded up", "The available balance refreshes when the send window opens"]}, {"v": "2.0.1", "items": ["Every transfer shows a confirm screen first: network, recipient, amount, fee and total", "Warnings for addresses that may be wrong; invalid addresses are blocked", "A safer wallet: outside links open only in your browser", "Tray icon to stop mining or quit the wallet", "Mining tab: graphics card check, network stats and pool mode", "New SCDO logo"]}, {"v": "2.0.0", "items": ["Release version, renamed to SCDO Wallet", "Accounts, settings and mining data are all kept"]}, {"v": "1.1.2 – 1.1.6", "items": ["Redesigned interface: big text, fewer buttons", "Switch to the SCDO Shard1–Shard4 (Classic) networks", "Accounts can be renamed, hidden and deleted (backed up first)", "The wallet checks for new versions", "Closing the wallet stops mining safely first"]}],
